  117: "# 117. Method Refrence, Constructor Refrence\n## 1. Overview of Method Refrence, Constructor Refrence\nModern Java (Java 8+) revolutionized the language by introducing functional programming constructs, declarative data pipelines via the Stream API, and modular enterprise database connectivity (JDBC).\n\n```\n                           MODERN JAVA ARCHITECTURE\n                                       │\n         ┌─────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┐\n         ▼                             ▼                             ▼\n    Lambda Expressions             Stream API                      JDBC\n  (p -> p.getAge() > 18)   .filter().map().collect()      Connection, PreparedStatement\n  Concise anonymous logic  Declarative data pipelines     Relational Database RDBMS\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Lambda Expressions & Stream API\n```java\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n\nList<String> languages = Arrays.asList(\"Java\", \"Python\", \"JavaScript\", \"C++\", \"Go\");\n\n// Declarative pipeline: filter languages starting with 'J', convert to uppercase, collect to list:\nList<String> jLangs = languages.stream()\n    .filter(lang -> lang.startsWith(\"J\"))\n    .map(String::toUpperCase)\n    .sorted()\n    .collect(Collectors.toList());\n\nSystem.out.println(jLangs); // [JAVA, JAVASCRIPT]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. JDBC Database Connectivity (PreparedStatement)\n```java\nimport java.sql.*;\n\npublic class DatabaseHelper {\n    public static void insertUser(int id, String name) throws SQLException {\n        String sql = \"INSERT INTO users (id, username) VALUES (?, ?)\";\n        try (Connection conn = DriverManager.getConnection(\"jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/app_db\", \"root\", \"secret\");\n             PreparedStatement stmt = conn.prepareStatement(sql)) {\n            stmt.setInt(1, id);\n            stmt.setString(2, name);\n            stmt.executeUpdate(); // Safe against SQL Injection attacks!\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 💡 Key Takeaway\nAlways prefer **`PreparedStatement`** over string concatenation to prevent SQL injection vulnerabilities. Use Java Streams for clean, readable, parallelizable data transformations.",

